# Rust
target/
core/target/
apps/**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# `Cargo.lock` is deliberately NOT ignored. This workspace builds binaries
# that are shipped (gateway, node, desktop sidecar), and an ignored lockfile
# means every machine resolves a different dependency graph: a developer
# builds against versions pinned in a months-old local lock while CI
# resolves the newest semver-compatible release of 91 crates and hits an API
# change nobody chose. "Green locally, red in CI" was that, not a code bug.
# Updating dependencies is a deliberate change now — `cargo update` in a PR,
# with the diff of the lock as the review surface.

# Desktop app build staging (populated by build.rs)
apps/acowork-desktop/src-tauri/bin/

